# o_\_jk swaps axes j and k (B17): transpose's own axis rule, so the
# other axes stay where they are. On a matrix o_\_12 is o_\; on a rank
# 3 array o_\_13 is o_\ too, and the order of the two digits does not
# matter.
== SOURCE
m := 2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6
a := 2 3 4 r_eshape r_ange 24
(o_\_12 m) m_atch o_\ m
s_hape o_\_23 a
1 s_elect o_\_23 a
s_hape o_\_12 a
(o_\_13 a) m_atch o_\ a
(o_\_32 a) m_atch o_\_23 a
== RESULT
1
2 4 3
1 5  9
2 6 10
3 7 11
4 8 12
3 2 4
1
1
